# Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in. Never commit `.dev.vars`.
#
# Secrets only. Non-secret behavior config lives in `wrangler.toml` under
# `[vars]` (TIMEZONE, START_HOUR/END_HOUR, PROCESS_MODE, ADMIN_USERNAMES,
# ADMIN_USER_IDS, ENABLE_FUNRESPONSE, MODERATION_PROMPT) and is picked up
# automatically by `wrangler dev`. Only put values here that must stay
# out of source control.
BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC-DEF-ghijklm
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-key-here

# Optional: verify Telegram webhook secret token (must match setWebhook --secret_token)
# Uncomment and set the same value you pass to `set-webhook`.
# WEBHOOK_SECRET_TOKEN=your-custom-secret

# Admin panel access token. Enables the /admin audit-log viewer (see
# ADMIN_PANEL_PATH in wrangler.toml). Keep it strong.
# ADMIN_PANEL_TOKEN=your-strong-random-token

# Optional: worker URL used by `npm run rotate-token` when no URL argument is
# passed (defaults to https://telegram-mod-bot.livenet123.workers.dev).
# WORKER_URL=https://telegram-mod-bot.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
